        '1970s-Present: Overtaken in popularity by Razz and Lowball Draw, but still played in home games and some card rooms.',
      ],
      evolution: 'The game maintained the simple structure of Five Card Stud while inverting the hand rankings. The ace-to-five system (A-2-3-4-5 as best hand) became standard, with straights and flushes not counting against the playerâ€”unlike deuce-to-seven lowball where they do count.',
      cultural: "More common in home games than casinos. Often played as part of mixed-game rotations or as a 'Dealer's Choice' option.",
